Adapted files: stabilizer.py, gpu_runtime.py, gpu_downloads.py, directml_pose.py,
and corresponding stabilization/GPU regression tests.
Pose session construction also builds on the original backend architecture.
Modifications: independent package/runtime/config namespaces; configurable
observation and smoothing settings; camera-oriented integration and tests.

The original test.22 baseline was a local uncommitted test version. A later
upstream default branch may differ; do not imply it is the exact source commit.

RTMPose preprocessing, inference interfaces and decoding use Tau-J/rtmlib
and OpenMMLab MMPose through their public APIs. Their implementations retain
their upstream licenses; model weights and optional runtimes are not bundled.

The GPU diagnostic uses ONNX Runtime's MIT-licensed tiny arithmetic graph.
Dependency and design-reference details appear in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md.
